IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gaa-dates`
IMPORT `gaa-rules`

-- Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) -- the questions of the ADULT FOR WHOM A GUARDIAN OR ADMINISTRATOR IS
-- SOUGHT OR APPOINTED.
--
-- SEAT: the individual the Act is applied to -- the adult with a disability who may lack decision-making capacity, for
-- whom a guardianship, administration or supportive order is sought or made (the proposed represented person, the
-- represented person, the supported person), including the person whose compensation or damages award is paid into
-- court and managed by an administrator. "Do I have decision-making capacity?", "Can VCAT appoint someone for me?",
-- "May my administrator collect my compensation?", "Where does the money the court awarded me go?", "What may my
-- administrator charge?", "Can I be compensated for my administrator's breach, and by when must I apply?". Where a
-- relative, carer or personal representative asks for the person, the questions are still worded from the person's
-- seat. Guardians, administrators, VCAT, the courts and the Public Advocate get no seat: their satisfaction, beliefs and
-- orders are asked as facts.
--
-- Every question takes plain facts (yes/no, numbers, dates, a choice from a list) and calls the rules of gaa-rules.l4.
-- The five deadline rules (ss 28, 37, 152, 164, 184) are DEONTIC rules run inside; no question takes a DEONTIC or EVENT.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Guardianship
-- and Administration Act 2019, Version No. 010 (15 April 2026), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria;
-- published with the authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced except
-- in accordance with the Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Guardianship and Administration Act 2019: the questions of the adult for whom a guardian or administrator is sought or appointed`

§§ `Disability, capacity and my nearest relative`

@export Do I have a disability within the Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) s 3? The Act means a neurological impairment, intellectual impairment, mental disorder, brain injury, physical disability or dementia. Orders under the Act can be sought only for a person with a disability.
GIVEN `impairment` IS A `Kind of impairment` @desc Your impairment, if any: a neurological impairment; an intellectual impairment; a mental disorder; a brain injury; a physical disability; dementia; or none of these
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Do I have a disability` MEANS
    `s 3 -- I have a disability` `impairment`

@export Do I have decision-making capacity for this matter (Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) s 5)? You are presumed to have it unless there is evidence to the contrary; otherwise you have it if, with any practicable and appropriate support, you can understand, retain, use or weigh the information and communicate the decision. Capacity is matter by matter and may be temporary.
GIVEN `evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is any evidence that you may not have capacity for this particular decision
      `appearance only` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that doubt rests only on your appearance, or only on a decision others think unwise
      `understand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can understand the information relevant to the decision and its effect, if it is explained in a way suited to you (simple language, visual aids or other means)
      `retain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can retain that information long enough to make the decision
      `weigh` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can use or weigh that information in making the decision
      `communicate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can communicate the decision and your views in some way (speech, gesture or other means), with any support you need
GIVETH A `Whether I have decision-making capacity`
`Do I have decision-making capacity` MEANS
    `s 5 -- my decision-making capacity` `evidence` `appearance only` `understand` `retain` `weigh` `communicate`

@export Who is my nearest relative (Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) s 3)? The first relative aged 18 or over in this order: spouse or domestic partner, child, parent, step-parent, sibling, step-sibling, grandparent, grandchild, uncle or aunt, nephew or niece; the eldest within a group. Your nearest relative may, for example, apply for compensation for you (s 183).
GIVEN `partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a spouse or domestic partner aged 18 or over
      `child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a child aged 18 or over
      `parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a living parent aged 18 or over
      `step-parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a step-parent aged 18 or over
      `sibling` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a brother or sister aged 18 or over (including one adopted by your parent)
      `step-sibling` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a step-brother or step-sister aged 18 or over
      `grandparent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a living grandparent
      `grandchild` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a grandchild aged 18 or over
      `uncle or aunt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have an uncle or aunt aged 18 or over
      `nephew or niece` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a nephew or niece aged 18 or over
GIVETH A `My nearest relative`
`Who is my nearest relative` MEANS
    `s 3 -- my nearest relative` `partner` `child` `parent` `step-parent` `sibling` `step-sibling` `grandparent` `grandchild` `uncle or aunt` `nephew or niece`

§§ `Applying for an order, and VCAT's power to make it`

@export Can someone apply to VCAT for a guardianship, administration, supportive guardianship or supportive administration order for me (Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) ss 22, 23, 79, 80)? Anyone may apply for an adult with a disability, or for someone under 18 if the order takes effect at 18. If you do not live in Victoria, a money order can cover only your property in Victoria.
GIVEN `order` IS A `Kind of order` @desc The order sought: a guardianship order (personal matters); an administration order (money and property); a supportive guardianship order; or a supportive administration order
      `impairment` IS A `Kind of impairment` @desc Your impairment, if any: a neurological impairment; an intellectual impairment; a mental disorder; a brain injury; a physical disability; dementia; or none of these
      `age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years
      `effect at 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are under 18: whether the order would take effect only when you turn 18 (answer yes if you are 18 or over)
      `lives in Victoria` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you live in Victoria
      `property in Victoria` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any of your property is in Victoria
GIVETH A `Whether an application can be made for me`
`Can someone apply for an order for me` MEANS
    `ss 22, 23, 79, 80 -- whether an application can be made for me` `order` `impairment` `age` `effect at 18` `lives in Victoria` `property in Victoria`

@export May VCAT appoint a guardian or an administrator for me (Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) ss 30, 31)? Only if VCAT is satisfied that, because of your disability, you lack decision-making capacity for the matter, that you need a guardian or administrator, and that the order will promote your personal and social wellbeing; and, for a money order when you live outside Victoria, that State Trustees is not already authorised over the property.
GIVEN `appointment` IS A `Kind of appointment` @desc Whether a guardian (personal matters) or an administrator (money and property) is sought
      `lacks capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT is satisfied that, because of your disability, you do not have decision-making capacity for the matter the order is sought for
      `in need` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT is satisfied you need a guardian or administrator (it considers your will and preferences, whether informal means or mediation would do, your family's and carers' wishes, and your existing relationships)
      `wellbeing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT is satisfied the order will promote your personal and social wellbeing
      `lives in Victoria` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you live in Victoria
      `State Trustees authorised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you live outside Victoria: whether State Trustees is already authorised under s 12 of the State Trustees (State Owned Company) Act 1994 over your property here (answer no otherwise)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May VCAT appoint a guardian or administrator for me` MEANS
    `s 30(2) -- VCAT may appoint a guardian or administrator for me` `appointment` `lacks capacity` `in need` `wellbeing` `lives in Victoria` `State Trustees authorised`

@export May VCAT appoint a supportive guardian or supportive administrator for me (Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) s 87)? Only if you consent, VCAT is satisfied that with practicable and appropriate support you will have decision-making capacity for the matter, and the order will promote your personal and social wellbeing. A supporter helps you decide; you keep the decision.
GIVEN `consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you consent to VCAT making the order
      `capacity with support` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT is satisfied that, given practicable and appropriate support, you will have decision-making capacity for the matter
      `wellbeing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT is satisfied the order will promote your personal and social wellbeing
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May VCAT appoint a supporter for me` MEANS
    `s 87(2) -- VCAT may appoint a supportive guardian or administrator for me` `consent` `capacity with support` `wellbeing`

@export Can this person be appointed as my guardian, administrator or supporter (Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) ss 32, 88)? An individual aged 18 or over (a company only as administrator) who consents, if VCAT is satisfied they will follow the Act's duties, are suitable, and (for a guardian or administrator) have no conflict of interest, and (for an administrator) have enough financial expertise. Being your relative, or disagreeing with another relative, does not by itself make someone conflicted or unsuitable.
GIVEN `order` IS A `Kind of order` @desc The order: a guardianship order; an administration order; a supportive guardianship order; or a supportive administration order
      `appointee` IS A `Kind of appointee` @desc Whether the proposed appointee is an individual or a body corporate (a company)
      `their age` IS A NUMBER @desc The proposed appointee's age in whole years (any number for a company)
      `consents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they consent to act
      `duties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT is satisfied they will act in accordance with the Act's duties
      `no conflict` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT is satisfied their interests do not and may not conflict with yours (not asked for a supporter)
      `suitable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT is satisfied they are suitable (it considers your will and preferences, your relationships, their availability, and preferring a relative or someone close to you)
      `expertise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an administrator: whether VCAT is satisfied they have sufficient expertise for the financial matters (answer yes otherwise)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can this person be appointed for me` MEANS
    `ss 32, 88 -- this person may be appointed for me` `order` `appointee` `their age` `consents` `duties` `no conflict` `suitable` `expertise`

§§ `Urgent orders and hearing times (only if an application has been made about me)`

@export What is the last day the urgent guardianship or administration order over me is in force (Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) s 36(3))? An urgent order lasts for the period it specifies, at most 21 days, and may be renewed once for at most 21 more days. No answer means the order specifies a longer period than the Act allows.
GIVEN `made on` IS A DATE @desc The day VCAT made the urgent order
      `days specified` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days the order says it is in force for
      `renewed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it has been renewed
      `renewal days` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days of the renewal (any number if not renewed)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`When does my urgent order end` MEANS
    `s 36(3) -- the last day my urgent order is in force` `made on` `days specified` `renewed` `renewal days`

@export Has VCAT held the full hearing after the urgent order over me in time (Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) s 37)? VCAT must hold a hearing, as soon as practicable but within 42 days after making the urgent order, to decide whether an ordinary order should be made.
GIVEN `made on` IS A DATE @desc The day VCAT made the urgent order
      `held` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the hearing has been held
      `held on` IS A DATE @desc The day it was held (any date if not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `Where the step stands`
`Has VCAT held the hearing after my urgent order in time` MEANS
    `s 37 -- where the hearing after my urgent order stands` `made on` `held` `held on` `today`

@export Has VCAT started hearing the application about me in time (Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) ss 28, 85)? VCAT must start within 30 days after the day it received the application, unless it required a compulsory conference or referred the matter to mediation.
GIVEN `conference or mediation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT or the principal registrar required a compulsory conference or referred the proceeding to mediation
      `received on` IS A DATE @desc The day VCAT received the application
      `started` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the hearing has started
      `started on` IS A DATE @desc The day it started (any date if not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `Where the step stands`
`Has VCAT started hearing the application about me in time` MEANS
    `s 28 -- where the start of my hearing stands` `conference or mediation` `received on` `started` `started on` `today`

§§ `What my guardian or administrator can do (only if an order is in force for me)`

@export Can my guardian or administrator do this for me (Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) ss 39, 53)? No order gives the power to make or revoke your will or enduring power of attorney, vote, consent to marriage, divorce or a sexual relationship, decide about the care or adoption of your child, enter a surrogacy arrangement or a substitute parentage order, manage your estate after your death, or consent to an unlawful act. Anything else depends on what the order specifies.
GIVEN `act` IS AN `Act done for me` @desc What they want to do: make or revoke your will; make or revoke your enduring power of attorney; vote for you; consent to your marriage, divorce or a sexual relationship; decide about the care or adoption of your child; enter into a surrogacy arrangement; consent to a substitute parentage order; manage your estate after your death; consent to an unlawful act; or something else
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my guardian or administrator do this for me` MEANS
    `ss 39, 53 -- my guardian or administrator can do this for me` `act`

@export May my administrator collect, receive and recover the compensation or damages for my injury (Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) ss 46, 52(a), 54, 69)? Yes if the administration order gives that power, or covers receiving money payable to you; the order lapses on your death or when you stop being a represented person, and the administrator's powers stop once the administrator knows.
GIVEN `state` IS A `Whether my administration order has ended` @desc Whether your administration order is in force, or has ended because you died or ceased to be a represented person
      `administrator knows` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it has ended: whether your administrator knows (answer no if it is in force)
      `s 52 power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the order specifies the power to collect, receive and recover compensation or damages for injury to you or your estate (s 52(a)(iii))
      `matter covers it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a financial matter in the order covers receiving and recovering money payable to you
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May my administrator collect my compensation or damages` MEANS
    `ss 46, 52, 54, 69 -- my administrator may collect my compensation or damages` `state` `administrator knows` `s 52 power` `matter covers it`

@export May my guardian or administrator bring, defend or settle a legal proceeding in my name, such as my compensation claim (Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) ss 38, 40, 51)? Only if VCAT specified that power in the order and the proceeding relates to a matter the order covers; they then need not be appointed litigation guardian.
GIVEN `appointment` IS A `Kind of appointment` @desc Whether it is your guardian (personal matters) or your administrator (money and property)
      `power specified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the order specifies the power to bring and defend actions and other legal proceedings
      `related` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the proceeding relates to a personal matter (guardian) or financial matter (administrator) specified in the order
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May my guardian or administrator bring a proceeding in my name` MEANS
    `ss 38, 40, 51 -- my guardian or administrator may bring or defend a proceeding in my name` `appointment` `power specified` `related`

@export Who pays the costs of a legal proceeding my guardian or administrator brought or defended for me (Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) ss 40(3)-(5), 51(3)-(5))? Your estate, unless a court or tribunal orders the guardian or administrator personally liable because they were negligent or engaged in misconduct.
GIVEN `personally liable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court or tribunal has ordered your guardian or administrator personally liable for the costs for negligence or misconduct
GIVETH A `Who pays the costs of my proceeding`
`Who pays the costs of my proceeding` MEANS
    `ss 40, 51 -- who pays the costs of my proceeding` `personally liable`

@export May my administrator make this gift from my property (Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) s 47)? Unless VCAT has ordered otherwise, only a gift that is reasonable in all the circumstances, including your finances, and is either a seasonal or special-event gift to your relative or close friend, or a donation of a kind you made, or might reasonably be expected to make. It may go to the administrator's own family or friends.
GIVEN `VCAT order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT has made an order about gifts from your property
      `reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the gift is reasonable in all the circumstances, including your financial circumstances
      `gift` IS A `Kind of gift` @desc The kind of gift: a seasonal or special-event gift (a birthday, a wedding) to your relative or close friend; a donation of a kind you made, or might reasonably be expected to make; or another kind of gift
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May my administrator make this gift` MEANS
    `s 47 -- my administrator may make this gift from my property` `VCAT order` `reasonable` `gift`

@export Must this gift from my property be detailed in my administrator's yearly account (Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) s 61(4)(b))? Yes if it went to the administrator, their relative or close friend, or an organisation connected with them, and is worth $100 or more (or the prescribed amount, if one is prescribed).
GIVEN `recipient` IS A `Who received the gift` @desc Who received it: your administrator; a relative or close friend of your administrator; an organisation connected with your administrator; or someone else
      `value` IS A NUMBER @desc The total value of the gift, in Australian dollars
      `prescribed` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount prescribed by regulations, in dollars, or 0 if none is prescribed
GIVETH A `Whether the gift must be detailed in the account`
`Must the gift be detailed in the account` MEANS
    `s 61(4)(b) -- whether the gift must be detailed in the account` `recipient` `value` `prescribed`

@export Is my administrator allowed to enter into a transaction in which they have a conflict of interest (Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) ss 57, 58)? Not if their duty to you may conflict with their own interests or those of their relative, business associate or close friend, unless it is a permitted gift, maintenance of your dependant, a dealing with property you hold jointly, or VCAT authorised it beforehand; VCAT may validate it afterwards.
GIVEN `conflict` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is, or may be, a conflict between your administrator's duty to you and their own interests or those of their relative, business associate or close friend
      `exception` IS A `Conflict exception` @desc Whether it is: no exception; a gift allowed under s 47; maintenance of your dependant under s 52(n); or a dealing with property you hold jointly with your administrator (or a loan or guarantee for it)
      `authorised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT authorised it (or transactions of that kind) at or before the time
      `validated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT has since validated it
GIVETH A `Whether my administrator's transaction is allowed`
`Is my administrator's conflict transaction allowed` MEANS
    `ss 57, 58 -- whether my administrator's transaction is allowed` `conflict` `exception` `authorised` `validated`

@export Is a dealing I made with my own money or property, or a contract I signed, void because of my administration order (Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) s 75)? Where the matter is under the order, without VCAT's order or your administrator's written consent you are taken to lack capacity for it, and the dealing is void and recoverable, unless the other person gave adequate value and proves they acted in good faith without knowing, or being able to know, of the order. Accepting payment of a debt counts as a dealing.
GIVEN `subject to order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the money, property or contract is a financial matter covered by your administration order
      `consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT made an order allowing it, or your administrator consented in writing
      `adequate consideration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other person gave adequate value (consideration) for it
      `good faith proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other person proves they acted in good faith and did not know, and could not reasonably have known, that you were under an administration order
GIVETH A `Whether my own dealing is void`
`Is my own dealing void` MEANS
    `s 75 -- whether my own dealing is void` `subject to order` `consent` `adequate consideration` `good faith proved`

@export When my guardian and my administrator disagree, whose decision prevails (Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) s 177)? The guardian's, unless they agreed otherwise or VCAT directed otherwise, and the administrator must take the steps needed to implement it, unless the administrator reasonably believes that would seriously deplete your estate, when the administrator must seek VCAT's advice instead.
GIVEN `otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your guardian and administrator agreed otherwise, or VCAT directed otherwise
      `depletion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your administrator reasonably believes implementing the guardian's decision is likely to seriously deplete your estate
GIVETH A `Whose decision prevails`
`Whose decision prevails` MEANS
    `s 177 -- whose decision prevails` `otherwise` `depletion`

@export May my supportive guardian or supportive administrator act to give effect to my decision (Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) ss 90, 93)? Only if the order gives that power, and never for a significant financial transaction: investments (except $10,000 or less in total in bank or other ADI interest-bearing accounts), real estate other than renting your own home, dealing with land, using your property as security, or buying or selling substantial personal property.
GIVEN `power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your supportive order gives the power to take action to give effect to your decisions (s 93)
      `transaction` IS A `Kind of transaction` @desc The decision: investing in interest-bearing accounts with a bank or other ADI; another investment; renting your own home; another real estate or land dealing; using your property as security; buying or selling substantial personal property; or another kind of decision
      `amount` IS A NUMBER @desc For an ADI investment: the total amount invested, in dollars (any number otherwise)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May my supporter give effect to my decision` MEANS
    `s 93 -- my supportive guardian or administrator may give effect to my decision` `power` `transaction` `amount`

§§ `My administrator's accounts and fees (only if an administration order is in force for me)`

@export When is my administrator's next yearly account due to VCAT (Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) s 61(2))? On, or as soon as practicable after, each anniversary of the appointment, unless VCAT has directed otherwise. The answer is the next anniversary on or after today.
GIVEN `appointed on` IS A DATE @desc The day your administrator was appointed
      `directed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT has directed a different time for the accounts
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`When is my administrator's next account due` MEANS
    `s 61(2) -- when my administrator's next yearly account is due` `appointed on` `directed otherwise` `today`

@export How much must my administrator make good for an item of the accounts VCAT disallowed (Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) s 61(5)-(7))? The amount of the item, if the examiner or auditor recommended disallowing it and VCAT ordered it disallowed; VCAT must not disallow it if satisfied the administrator acted in good faith and with reasonable care.
GIVEN `recommended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person examining or auditing the accounts recommended disallowing the item
      `good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT is satisfied your administrator acted in good faith and with reasonable care
      `disallowed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT has ordered the item disallowed
      `amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of the item, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What must my administrator make good` MEANS
    `s 61(6), (7) -- what my administrator must make good for a disallowed item` `recommended` `good faith` `disallowed` `amount`

@export What may my administrator charge my estate for acting (Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) ss 95, 175)? A family member or other non-professional administrator nothing, unless VCAT specified it in the order; a professional on the scale in the VCAT rules or as VCAT determines (a licensed trustee company within the Corporations Act Chapter 5D limit); a supportive guardian or administrator nothing at all.
GIVEN `administrator` IS A `Who my administrator is` @desc Who your administrator is: a supportive guardian or supportive administrator; a licensed trustee company; another person who carries on a business of administering estates; or anyone else (for example a family member)
      `specified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT specified remuneration in the administration order
GIVETH A `What my administrator may charge`
`What may my administrator charge` MEANS
    `ss 95, 175 -- what my administrator may charge` `administrator` `specified`

§§ `When my order ends (only if I have died or stopped being a represented person)`

@export How much money must my administrator pay to me, or my personal representative, when the order ends (Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) s 71)? All the money standing to your credit, less any amount due to the administrator and the costs, expenses and liabilities they incurred. No answer means the order has not ended.
GIVEN `ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the order has ended (you died or ceased to be a represented person) and your administrator has been told
      `credit` IS A NUMBER @desc The money standing to your credit with your administrator, in dollars
      `due` IS A NUMBER @desc The amounts due to your administrator and the costs, expenses and liabilities they incurred, in dollars
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much must my administrator pay over` MEANS
    `s 71 -- the money my administrator must pay over` `ended` `credit` `due`

@export May I inspect my former administrator's books and accounts and get copies (Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) ss 72, 73)? Yes, once you have stopped being a represented person (or as your personal representative), unless VCAT has ordered the document withheld from you.
GIVEN `ceased` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have ceased to be a represented person (or you are asking as the personal representative of one who has died)
      `withheld` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT has ordered the document withheld from you
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May I inspect my former administrator's records` MEANS
    `ss 72, 73 -- I may inspect my former administrator's records` `ceased` `withheld`

@export May my former administrator sell a personal effect of mine that I have not claimed (Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) s 74)? Only after public notice, and only if you have not claimed it within 2 years after the day you stopped being a represented person; the proceeds go to the Consolidated Fund.
GIVEN `ceased on` IS A DATE @desc The day you ceased to be a represented person
      `claimed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have claimed the item
      `notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your former administrator has given public notice
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`May my former administrator sell my unclaimed effects` MEANS
    `s 74 -- my former administrator may sell my unclaimed personal effect` `ceased on` `claimed` `notice` `today`

§§ `Damages or compensation a court orders paid to me (only if I have a claim in court)`

@export Where does money a court orders paid to me go, such as damages or a compensation award (Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) s 179(3), (8))? If the Supreme, County or Magistrates' Court orders money paid to a person with a disability in a civil proceeding, it is paid into court and then, unless the court orders otherwise, paid out to your administrator or, if you have none, State Trustees; that order works as an administration order.
GIVEN `court` IS A `Which court` @desc The court: the Supreme Court; the County Court; the Magistrates' Court; or another court or tribunal
      `civil` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a civil proceeding
      `impairment` IS A `Kind of impairment` @desc Your impairment, if any: a neurological impairment; an intellectual impairment; a mental disorder; a brain injury; a physical disability; dementia; or none of these
      `ordered otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has ordered something else about paying the money out
      `has administrator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have an administrator
GIVETH A `Where the money a court awards me goes`
`Where does the money a court awards me go` MEANS
    `s 179(3) -- where the money a court awards me goes` `court` `civil` `impairment` `ordered otherwise` `has administrator`

@export Can the court hearing my claim refer to VCAT whether I need a guardian, administrator or supporter (Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) s 179(1), (2))? Yes, in a civil proceeding in the Supreme, County or Magistrates' Court, if the court considers that you, as a party, may need one; the referral is treated as an application to VCAT.
GIVEN `court` IS A `Which court` @desc The court: the Supreme Court; the County Court; the Magistrates' Court; or another court or tribunal
      `civil` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a civil proceeding
      `party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a party to the proceeding
      `may need` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court considers you may need a guardian, supportive guardian, administrator or supportive administrator
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the court refer my case to VCAT` MEANS
    `s 179(1) -- the court hearing my claim may refer my need for a guardian or administrator to VCAT` `court` `civil` `party` `may need`

§§ `Compensation from my guardian or administrator (only if I suffered a loss through their breach)`

@export Can my guardian or administrator be ordered to compensate me for a loss they caused (Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) ss 181, 182, 186)? The Supreme Court or VCAT may order it for a loss caused by their contravening the Act while acting, even if they were convicted, the order has ended, or you have died (then to your estate); they may be relieved of all or part if they acted honestly and reasonably and ought fairly to be excused. The State pays no compensation.
GIVEN `contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the loss was caused by your guardian or administrator contravening the Act while acting as such
      `relief` IS A `Relief from liability` @desc Whether the Supreme Court or VCAT has relieved them: no relief; relieved of part; or relieved of all
      `died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have died (the question is then asked for your estate)
GIVETH A `Whether I can be compensated`
`Can I be compensated by my guardian or administrator` MEANS
    `ss 181, 182 -- whether I can be compensated` `contravention` `relief` `died`

@export Can this person apply for compensation from my guardian or administrator for me (Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) s 183)? You (or a former represented person), your personal representative, the executor or administrator of your estate, the Public Advocate, your nearest relative, or someone the Supreme Court or VCAT finds has a special interest in your affairs.
GIVEN `applicant` IS A `Who is applying for compensation` @desc Who is applying: you; your personal representative; the executor or administrator of your estate; the Public Advocate; your nearest relative; someone the Supreme Court or VCAT determines has a special interest in your affairs; or someone else
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can this person apply for compensation for me` MEANS
    `s 183 -- this person may apply for compensation for me` `applicant`

@export By when must an application for compensation from my guardian or administrator be made (Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) s 184)? Within 6 months after your death, or theirs, or the first of the two deaths; the Supreme Court or VCAT may extend the time. While both of you are alive the Act sets no time limit (no answer).
GIVEN `I died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have died (asked for your estate)
      `my death` IS A DATE @desc The day you died (any date if not)
      `they died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your guardian or administrator has died
      `their death` IS A DATE @desc The day they died (any date if not)
      `extended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court or VCAT has extended the time
      `extended to` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the extended time (any date if not extended)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`By when must I apply for compensation` MEANS
    `s 184 -- the last day to apply for compensation from` (`s 184(1) -- the day of the first death` `I died` `my death` `they died` `their death`) `extended` `extended to`

@export Is the application for compensation from my guardian or administrator in time (Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) s 184)? It must be made within 6 months after the first relevant death (yours or theirs), or within any time the Supreme Court or VCAT allows; while both of you are alive the Act sets no limit.
GIVEN `I died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have died (asked for your estate)
      `my death` IS A DATE @desc The day you died (any date if not)
      `they died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your guardian or administrator has died
      `their death` IS A DATE @desc The day they died (any date if not)
      `extended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court or VCAT has extended the time
      `extended to` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the extended time (any date if not extended)
      `applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the application has been made
      `applied on` IS A DATE @desc The day it was made (any date if not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `Where the step stands`
`Is my compensation application in time` MEANS
    `s 184 -- where my compensation application stands` (`s 184(1) -- the day of the first death` `I died` `my death` `they died` `their death`) `extended` `extended to` `applied` `applied on` `today`

@export What is the maximum penalty if my guardian, administrator or supporter dishonestly uses the order to gain money or cause me loss (Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) ss 188-192)? 5 years' imprisonment or 600 penalty units or both; a company acting as administrator 2300 penalty units. The answer is in penalty units; 0 years means no imprisonment.
GIVEN `offender` IS A `Who used the order dishonestly` @desc Who used the order dishonestly: your guardian; your administrator; your supportive guardian; or your supportive administrator
      `company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offender is a body corporate (a company)
GIVETH A MAYBE `Maximum penalty`
`What is the maximum penalty for dishonest use of my order` MEANS
    `ss 188-192 -- the maximum penalty for using the order dishonestly against me` `offender` `company`

§§ `Rehearings and reassessments (only if VCAT has made an order about me)`

@export Can I apply to VCAT for a rehearing of an order made about me (Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) ss 150, 151, 153)? A party may (you are always a party), and a person entitled to notice may with VCAT's leave; after a reassessment VCAT started itself, only with leave. There is no rehearing of an order made by VCAT constituted by the President, or of a rehearing or leave application, and urgent orders appointing a guardian or administrator are excluded.
GIVEN `role` IS A `My role in the proceeding` @desc Your role: you were a party; you were entitled to notice but not a party; or neither
      `order` IS A `The order to be reheard` @desc The order: an order on an application; an urgent order appointing a guardian or administrator; an order on a reassessment VCAT conducted on its own initiative; an order on a reassessment someone applied for; or an order on an application for a rehearing or for leave
      `President` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT was constituted by its President (with or without others) when it made the order
GIVETH A `Whether I can apply for a rehearing`
`Can I apply for a rehearing` MEANS
    `ss 150, 151, 153 -- whether I can apply for a rehearing` `role` `order` `President`

@export By when must I apply for a rehearing, or for leave to apply, of a VCAT order made about me (Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) s 152)? Within 28 days after the day of the order; if VCAT gave oral reasons and a party then asked for written reasons, the 28 days run from the day the written reasons were given. The Act gives no power to extend.
GIVEN `made on` IS A DATE @desc The day VCAT made the order
      `written reasons requested` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT gave oral reasons and a party then requested written reasons
      `reasons given on` IS A DATE @desc The day the written reasons were given (any date if none were requested)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I apply for a rehearing` MEANS
    `the date` 28 `days after` (`s 152(2) -- the day of the order` `made on` `written reasons requested` `reasons given on`)

@export Is my application for a rehearing, or for leave to apply, in time (Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) s 152)? It must be made within 28 days after the day of the order (or of the written reasons, if requested after oral reasons).
GIVEN `made on` IS A DATE @desc The day VCAT made the order
      `written reasons requested` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT gave oral reasons and a party then requested written reasons
      `reasons given on` IS A DATE @desc The day the written reasons were given (any date if none were requested)
      `applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have applied
      `applied on` IS A DATE @desc The day you applied (any date if not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `Where the step stands`
`Is my rehearing application in time` MEANS
    `s 152 -- where my rehearing application stands` (`s 152(2) -- the day of the order` `made on` `written reasons requested` `reasons given on`) `applied` `applied on` `today`

@export By when must VCAT next reassess the order over me (Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) s 159(2))? Within 12 months after the order was made, and then at least once in each 3-year period counted from the making of the order, unless VCAT orders otherwise (no answer). The answer is the last day.
GIVEN `made on` IS A DATE @desc The day VCAT made the order
      `ordered otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT has ordered a different timetable for reassessment
      `reassessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT has reassessed the order at least once
      `latest reassessment` IS A DATE @desc The day of the latest reassessment (any date if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`By when must VCAT next reassess my order` MEANS
    `s 159(2) -- the last day for VCAT's next reassessment of my order` `made on` `ordered otherwise` `reassessed` `latest reassessment`

@export Have I asked in time for a hearing of VCAT's reassessment of my order (Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) s 164(4)-(6))? Where VCAT notifies that it will reassess the order on the papers without changing it, you have 14 days after the date of the notice to ask in writing for a hearing; if no one asks, VCAT need not hold one.
GIVEN `notice dated` IS A DATE @desc The date of VCAT's notice
      `requested` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have requested a hearing in writing
      `requested on` IS A DATE @desc The day you requested it (any date if not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `Where the step stands`
`Have I asked for a reassessment hearing in time` MEANS
    `s 164 -- where my request for a reassessment hearing stands` `notice dated` `requested` `requested on` `today`
